    {
      "source_id": "S2",
      "chunk_id": "F04-053772e0634e9843d4e8becb9b1d255bda71ca64423f1f231cf347f82c060101",
      "document_id": "F04",
      "text": "New self-service actions\n\n- Employees now submit correction requests from their own attendance timeline. The window is 14 calendar days and payroll must be unlocked. One pending request per workday is allowed. Managers approve or reject; approval recalculates within five minutes. HR Payroll handles locked or older periods, replacing the former direct manager-edit route.\n- Employees now cancel pending or approved annual leave themselves before the first scheduled shift starts. Cancellation immediately releases the reserved or deducted balance and notifies the manager. Started leave still requires HR review. Employees no longer need to contact HR Support for every cancellation.\n- Employees can propose a swap at least 24 hours before the earlier shift starts. The colleague must accept within 12 hours; the manager then approves. Until approval updates both assignments, the original roster applies. Team, skill, overlap, 11-hour rest and weekly-hour checks apply. Unaccepted proposals expire after 12 hours or at the earlier shift start, whichever comes first.",
      "token_count": 188,
